      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given series, $1+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1 \\cdot 3}{3 \\cdot 6}+\\frac{1 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5}{3 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 9}+\\frac{1 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7}{3 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 12}+\\ldots \\infty$\r\n$=1+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{3}{2}}{1 \\cdot 2}\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{3}{1 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 3} \\cdot \\frac{5}{3}\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{3} \\ldots \\infty$\r\n$=1+\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}+1\\right)}{2 !}\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{2}+\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}+1\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{2}+2\\right)}{3 !}$\r\n$=\\left(1-\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{-1 / 2}=3^{1 / 2}=\\sqrt{3}$",
    "image": null
  },
